Add missing -lrapidcheck linker flag to libexpr-tests (nix 2.14–2.15)

nix 2.14 introduced rapidcheck as a property-test dependency and added it to
buildInputs, but forgot to add -lrapidcheck to libexpr-tests_LDFLAGS in
src/libexpr/tests/local.mk. The same flag was correctly present in
libstore-tests/local.mk and libutils-tests/local.mk from the start.

Without this flag the libexpr-tests binary fails to link on macOS (where the
linker does not search transitively) with:
  ld: symbol(s) not found for architecture x86_64: _rapidcheck::*

Fixed upstream in nix 2.16.

--- a/src/libexpr/tests/local.mk
+++ b/src/libexpr/tests/local.mk
@@ -16,4 +16,4 @@

 libexpr-tests_LIBS = libstore-tests libutils-tests libexpr libutil libstore libfetchers

-libexpr-tests_LDFLAGS := $(GTEST_LIBS) -lgmock
+libexpr-tests_LDFLAGS := -lrapidcheck $(GTEST_LIBS) -lgmock
